Z||000011||mrfixit58||12-14-2000||05:39 PM||||Here's a couple of things to chew on:<P>1.3 million registered voters in Philly... 1 million voted (77%). I find it hard to believe.<P>Letters with ballots  were sent to over 1 million illegal aliens in California from Clinton asking them to vote Democrate.<P>Democrates claim Gore won the popular vote but, almost 1 million absentee ballots were not counted in California (because Gore won over Bush by 1.2 million votes). If the national average of 2-to-1 absentee votes go republican, that means 600,000 votes to Bush and 300,000 to Gore.  That evens things up in the popular vote. Now throw in all the other states UN-COUNTED absentee votes (remember the democrate montra of "count every vote") and I would be willing to bet that Bush then leads in the "Popular Vote" category.<P>Makes ya wonder,<BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||3
Z||000012||Tigger||12-14-2000||07:36 PM||||<B>IT'S NOT OVER, GORE CAN STILL BECOME THE NEXT PRESIDENT!!!</B><P>All he would have to do is round up enough Republicans along with Supreme Court Justice Rehnquist, and waste another 50 million taxpaying dollars and try to impeach Clinton!  Then Gore would be the next President!<P>I say Republicans and Democrats, let's unite and impeach Clinton, we still have time!!!<P>Awe well, I can't wait till tax time.  Can't wait to get that HUGE tax refund I was promised.      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">  I guess I'll have to keep waiting.     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Hey now guys, come on now, tell the entire country all of your alleged sexual relations with all of woman you have been with over the past 8 years.  Knowing all of you, you're answer would probably be "TO GO TO HELL!"  Get my point?  No you don't have to tell us, I'm just kidding, that is YOUR BUSINESS I don't think anyone here wants to know.<P>mrfixit58, I see your point.  But there are just too many votes, and not enough time to hand count them all.  Bush would have probably stepped in and made another appeal to the Supreme Court against counting those votes anyway.  Sorry   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>I think the country should keep electing the stupid one.  I'd hate to have a President in office who is better than I am.     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 12-14-2000).]||||reg||3
Z||000013||BN Boomer||12-14-2000||09:18 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>But there are just too many votes, and not enough time to hand count them all. <HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Okay, so I guess as a good Democrat you only want to count, recount, recount, recount, and then recount again the ones that are most likely to benefit your candidate. Sures sound like following the "Every vote counts" mantra to me... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000014||Tigger||12-14-2000||10:49 PM||||BN, LoL.  You're quoting a sentence I used in a sarcastic mannor, but actually heard repeatedly from many good Republicans.  Now that doesn't sound like the "Every vote counts" mantra to me either.<P>I think you need to understand a little more on how the election procedures are actually written and how they go on in Florida before you make assumptions about people.<P>According to Florida state Laws...<BR><A HREF="http://www.leg.state.fl.us/statutes/index.cfm?App_mode=Display_Statute&Search_String=&URL=Ch0102/SEC166.HTM&Title=-&gt;2000-&gt;Ch0102-&gt;Section%20166" TARGET=_blank>102.166  Protest of election returns; procedure.--<BR></A><P>In the procedure, each canidate is ALLOWED to have hand re-counts in up to 3 precinct (See #4d)  Al Gore chose his 3 precincts, by law this was his right.  If you feel this "selective counting" should not be allowed, I urge you by all means to go appeal the Florida Laws.<P>Most states allow an all state hand re-count.  We have had a statewide hand re-count here in Michigan for a House seat for this election, and Gov. George Bush had passed a law in Texas that allows hand re-counts in ALL counties in the event of a close election.  It sounds simple, but Florida <B>does not</B>.<P>My point is, it was all perfectly legal for Gore to select the re-counted precincts that would best benefit his interests.<P>I guess if Bush really trusted the voters in Florida he would have come forward asking for an immediate statewide manual re-count to settle the election once and for all even thought the state government wasn't obligated to do.<P>BTW, did anyone happen to notice Pres. Elect George Bush forgot to thank Jeb Bush last night in his acceptance speech?  He should at least offer him a spot in his cabinet.       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 12-14-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000015||Phil||12-14-2000||10:59 PM||||It's against the law to appoint a close relative to a cabinet post||||reg||1
